{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1377453-suggested-ship-names-for-the-leviathan-jump-ships","id":1377453,"title":"Suggested ship names for the Leviathan jump ships","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-30T22:30:11-07:00","id":1377453,"title":"Suggested ship names for the Leviathan jump ships","content":"According to Trinity: Aeon, page 307, there are fewer than 2 dozen Leviathan jump ships. Waaaaay back in the day of the original Aeon Trinity, I took it upon myself to make a list of published Leviathan names used in the original books. There weren't very many, certainly not anywhere near all 24 (as I recall, in the original Trinity book, it was mentioned that less than 30 Leviathans existed), but I thought I'd post the list I made here, just in case anyone needed inspiration for what to name their jump ship.<br /> <br /> UNS Meroe<br /> <br /> UNS Svaha<br /> <br /> UNS Ananda<br /> <br /> UNS Shaka<br /> <br /> UNS Mae de C\u00e9u<br /> <br /> UNS Kohl<br /> <br /> UNS Pandora<br /> <br /> UNS Yi<br /> <br /> UNS Iroqatsi<br /> <br /> UNS Chicago<br /> <br /> UNS Mabuhay (I included this name as per the recent publication of &quot;Leviathan Mabuhay&quot;)<br /> <br /> UNS Sava (Sources: Distant Worlds (p.43))<br /> <br /> UNS Melbourne (Sources: Distant Worlds (p.80); AEon Ready Made Characters (p.5))<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I didn't think to record the sources of which original Trinity books referenced these names, but I expect Extrasolar Colonies, Alien Races and perhaps the Upeo wa Macho books would have the bulk of the references in them. Here's hoping you find this useful.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Added Sava and Melbourne to the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 03-31-2020, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T23:10:57-07:00","id":1377456,"title":"","content":"Oh nice work, interesting didn't know they mentioned so many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T00:23:10-07:00","id":1377466,"title":"","content":"Distant Worlds has the <i>Sava</i> (p.43), and the <i>Melbourne</i> appears there (p.80) and in AEon Ready Made Characters (p.5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 03-31-2020, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reacti